<title>AUSTRIA: VA Tech units get big China order.</title>
<headline>VA Tech units get big China order.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elin Energieversorgung and Voest-Alpine MCE, both units of Austria's VA Tech, said on Tuesday they had received a big order to equip a hydroelectric power plant in the Chinese province of Guangdong.</p>
<p>The two companies' share of the total investment of around eight billion schillings would be nearly 10 percent, VA Tech said in a statement.</p>
<p>Elin will be in charge of electrically equipping the plant and will deliver four generators and the electric equipment, while Voest-Alpine MCE will deliver four turbines and the mechanical equipment.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
</text>
